{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:80512",
  "title": "Moderate: curl security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-15 00:08:46"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-20 00:12:09"
  },
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "The curl packages provide the libcurl library and the curl utility for downloading files from servers using various protocols, including HTTP, FTP, and LDAP.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* curl: curl: Proxy credential disclosure via redirects to unauthenticated proxies (CVE-2026-6253)\n\n* curl: libcurl: Authentication bypass due to incorrect HTTP Negotiate connection reuse (CVE-2026-5545)\n\n* curl: libcurl: Credential leak via reused proxy connection during HTTP redirects (CVE-2026-6429)\n\n* curl: libcurl: Information disclosure via incorrect Proxy-Authorization header reuse (CVE-2026-7168)\n\n* libcurl: libcurl: Use-after-free vulnerability leading to Denial of Service (CVE-2026-10536)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
